<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wilhelmine of Bayreuth</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1709–1758</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Wilhelmine of Prussia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wilhelmine of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayreuth">Bayreuth</a> was a Prussian princess, the favourite sister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-the-great">Frederick the Great</a>, who married Margrave Frederick of Brandenburg-Bayreuth in 1731. A composer, writer and patron, she made Bayreuth a centre of the arts, building the Margravial Opera House and remodelling the Hermitage palace. Her memoirs give a lively picture of the Prussian court.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wilhelmine-of-bayreuth.jpg" alt="Wilhelmine of Bayreuth" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean-Étienne Liotard · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jean-Etienne_Liotard_-_Portr%C3%A4t_der_Markgr%C3%A4fin_Wilhelmine_von_Bayreuth.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
